.TH BCL 1 "2026-11-24" "BCL-32 1.2" "BCL-32 Manual"
.SH NAME
bcl \- interpreter for the Basic Command Language 32 (BCL-32)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bcl
[\fB\-\-restricted\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-rc\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-root\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR] [\fIscript.bcl\fR [\fIargs\fR...]]
.br
.B bcl \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bcl
runs a BCL-32 script, or starts an interactive session (REPL) when no script
is given. BCL-32 is a small text-based scripting language. Everything is a
string; numeric work goes through
.BR CALC .
Strings and lists are indexed from 1. List elements that contain spaces are
wrapped in braces:
.BR "one {two words} three" .
Booleans: the empty string and
.B 0
are false; any other value is true.
.PP
Before anything else the interpreter runs
.B $HOME/.bcl.rc
if it exists (see
.BR "STARTUP FILE" ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and build number (\fBBCL-32 v1.2 build N\fR) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rc
Do not read the startup file.
.TP
.B \-\-restricted
Restricted mode: disables
.B LOAD
and
.BR UNLOAD ;
.B SOURCE
is only allowed inside the source root.
.TP
.BI \-\-source\-root " DIR"
Directory in which
.B SOURCE
is allowed in restricted mode.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options; the next word is the script.
.SH LANGUAGE SUMMARY
.TP
.B Variables
.BR SET ", " INCR " (optional negative or decimal delta), " INCRV ", " GLOBAL
(one name per line), \fBEXISTS\fR, \fBUNSET\fR. Substitution:
.B $name
and
.BR [command\ ...] .
Associative arrays use names like
.BR name(key) ,
managed with
.BR ARREXISTS ", " ARRLENG ", " ARRKEYS ", " ARRGET ", " ARRSET ", " ARRDEL ", " ARRCLEAR .
.TP
.B Control
.B IF ... THEN [ELSEIF|ELSE] ... END
is the conditional;
.B IF ... DO ... LOOP
is the (only) loop. Its
.B ELSE
runs only if the loop ended naturally, not on
.BR BREAK .
.BR BREAK " and " NEXT
act on the nearest loop.
.TP
.B Input/output
.BR PUTS ", " PUTSN ", " GETS .
.TP
.B Numbers
.B CALC
evaluates real and complex expressions (bases 2, 8, 10 and 16).
.TP
.B Strings
.BR STRLENG ", " STRGET ", " STRRANG ", " STRFIND ", " STRAPP ", " STRINS ", " STRDEL ", "
.BR STRFMT " (one validated specifier), " STRUPP ", " STRLOW ", " STRREV ", " STREQ .
.TP
.B Lists
.BR LSTLENG ", " LSTGET ", " LSTRANG ", " LSTFIND ", " LSTAPP ", " LSTINS ", " LSTDEL ", " LSTSORT ", " LSTFMT .
.TP
.B Procedures
.B PROC name WITH a b @opt DO ... END
with
.BR RETURN .
Parameters marked with
.B @
are optional.
.TP
.B Errors
.B TRY ... CATCH var ... END
and
.BR "ERROR message" .
Diagnostics look like
.BR "?FAC-SEV-CODE, summary" ;
inside
.B CATCH
the array
.B var_INFO(...)
exposes FACILITY, CODE, FILE, LINE, COL, PROC and TRACE.
.TP
.B Program and modules
.B EXIT
ends the program.
.B SOURCE file
runs another script in the current scope.
.B LOAD module.bll
and
.B UNLOAD
manage native modules (distributed separately). A module name without
.B /
is searched in the comma-separated directories of the variable
.B BCL_LIBS
(first match wins); a name with
.B /
is used as written.
.TP
.B $ARGS
The program arguments, as a BCL list.
.SH STARTUP FILE
.B $HOME/.bcl.rc
is executed before the script, any
.B SOURCE
or the REPL. An error in it ends the interpreter with status 1. It is skipped
with
.BR \-\-no\-rc ,
with
.BR BCL_NO_RC=1 ,
and in restricted mode.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BCL_LIBS
Initial value of the variable
.BR BCL_LIBS .
.TP
.B BCL_NO_RC
If set and not
.BR 0 ,
the startup file is not read.
.TP
.B BCL_RESTRICTED
.B 1
enables restricted mode.
.TP
.B BCL_SOURCE_ROOT
Source root for restricted mode.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on an uncaught error; the code given to
.B EXIT
otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
SET n 5
PUTS "double: [CALC $n * 2]"
.fi
.PP
More programs in the \fBexamples/\fR directory (installed in
\fBshare/bcl/examples\fR). The full manual is \fBdoc/manual.md\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $HOME/.bcl.rc
Startup file.
